        "sha256": "c3dd3c12d7930af5871e2f348178ae067c3cb1759e39c855d3a8312556336226"
      },
      "reason": "Final-review qualification of the historical #260 dilution rationale: the original CCAP PE footnote explicitly says to filter natural seawater, reduce it to 95% using glass distilled water, and autoclave. That prepared input is then dosed at 950 cm3; the prior dilution is not inferred from the receiving-medium dose. The literal 95%-strength label is retained as REJECTED_LABEL on this bare filtered-seawater owner, without inventing the percentage basis, final volume, component ratio or a new preparation owner. The unqualified Natural seawater alias is also nonresolving: its recovered JCM1377 contexts state natural seawater without filtration. Supported Filtered natural seawater and Natural seawater (filtrated) aliases remain. Earlier #260 mapping evidence and histories are preserved as historical rationale, superseded only on these alias applicability points by this source-backed qualification. The two assigned filtered cases are not reinterpreted as the 95% preparation. Sources: https://www.ccap.ac.uk/wp-content/uploads/MR_PE.pdf ; https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=1377 .",
      "finding_ids": [
        "W04-BIO-HOLD-01"
      ]
    },
